<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    1. The jet's build cost: its shell (Patches 0.30.0). Its parts, the engine, nozzles, landing gear, tanks, electrics, hydraulics and avionics,
    come from its parts bill (Defs/Bill_HarrierVtol.xml), filled by RimThunder's or our own parts, as Close Air Support's jets are. Stock: 450
    steel, 150 plasteel, 25 components, 6 advanced components and a Vanilla Vehicles Expanded engine block. The shell keeps the airframe's
    steel, plasteel standing for its composites (about a quarter of the real airframe's weight), and the components the bill's parts do not
    carry. All AUTHORED. Steel stays FIRST: Vehicle Framework reads the first cost item for the jet's destruction sound. Before 0.30.0 this
    asked for car exhausts, wheels and suspension, and RimThunder's turbine only with RimThunder's research.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleBuildDef[defName="Harrier_Jet_Blueprint"]/costList</xpath>
    <value>
      <costList>
        <Steel>400</Steel>
        <Plasteel>120</Plasteel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>10</ComponentIndustrial>
      </costList>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- 2. The Hind and Mongoose both ask for construction skill 10; a jet shouldn't ask for less. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleBuildDef[defName="Harrier_Jet_Blueprint"]/constructionSkillPrerequisite</xpath>
    <value>
      <constructionSkillPrerequisite>10</constructionSkillPrerequisite>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!-- 3. Drop Tanks: the shell, steel for the pylon fittings (authored); its two fuel tanks come from the parts bill (Patches 0.30.0; before,
       two of Vanilla Vehicles Expanded's car fuel tanks). Stock: 60 steel, 2 components. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.UpgradeTreeDef[defName="Harrier_UpgradeTree"]/nodes/li[key="Harrier_DropTanks"]/ingredients</xpath>
    <value>
      <ingredients>
        <Steel>20</Steel>
        <ComponentIndustrial>2</ComponentIndustrial>
      </ingredients>
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <!--
    4. The fuel tank's radius is an int, so "2.5" logs "Parsed 2.5 as int" at every start. The game truncates it to 2
    (ParseHelper.ParseIntPermissive), so writing 2 changes only the warning. Guarded on the value, so a later fix by
    the mod's author is left alone.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="Harrier_Jet"]/components/li[key="FuelTank"]/reactors/li[@Class="Vehicles.Reactor_Explosive"]/radius[.="2.5"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/Vehicles.VehicleDef[defName="Harrier_Jet"]/components/li[key="FuelTank"]/reactors/li[@Class="Vehicles.Reactor_Explosive"]/radius</xpath>
      <value>
        <radius>2</radius>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
